    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6696966c5a0dd76d0467299d744be55419970bbed5b41948cd986366a3777867",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source builds a staged bridge from the off-diagonal mean-value terms to tractable oscillatory integrals. Reindexing pairs by their additive difference defines the shifted series f; separating explicit pole-bearing pieces yields a corrected function g; Poisson summation rewrites g as a divisor-weighted transform series; the divisor summatory decomposition and boundary estimates continue g(u,1-u); and integrating the resulting critical product separates the residual mean value into I1-I4 for component-specific asymptotic analysis.",
