    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_847aaf6abcde452725306bb2f3971b7c1898ca1dac840c81b825701be4e35be7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the stationary main-term sums in these applications, the cutoff records phase geometry: an index contributes a saddle term only when its transformed phase has an interior critical point satisfying the interval and sign conditions. When that condition fails, the stationary contribution is omitted while endpoint or nonstationary error terms remain. In the J_n application this criterion produces a provisional transition index Z, whose neighboring and tail ranges must be bounded before Z can be replaced by the explicit final cutoff.",
