    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c16041e179c68650e9624c30f31ec426ea277ceb255679dea63cfeaa7572c803",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The two oscillatory families use saddle analysis at different representational depths. The first is produced by applying the specialized logarithmic-phase lemma directly to I1, while the second is produced only after I4's inner kernel is saddle-reduced, the Voronoi-type oscillatory expansion of the divisor remainder is inserted, the result is rewritten as integrals J_n, and a second saddle criterion selects the contributing indices before transition-range estimates complete the finite sum.",
